--   Chapter 10 two-variable Hahn series: theta series, $\mathrm{Rho}$, Zwegers and Hickerson lemmas, (10.15) sum
-- statement:
--   This large bundle sets up the rings $K=\mathbb{Q}((Q))$ and $S$ of two-variable Hahn series with exponents $Q^ax^iy^j$ in lexicographic order ($Q$ first), monomials, coefficient extraction (including slices $[x^iy^j]$ and the constant term in $x,y$), and the embedding $K\to S$. It defines theta series $\sum(-1)^nQ^{AT(n)+en}x^{in}y^{jn}$ with $T(n)=n(n-1)/2$, the $q=Q^3$ specializations $\Theta(x;q)$, $\Theta(y;q)$, $\Theta(xy;q)$, Euler's $(q;q)_\infty$ as an element of $K$, and the Zwegers-lemma series and their right sides. It also defines the sign function $\rho$, $\mathrm{Rho}=\sum\rho(r,s)Q^{3rs}x^ry^s$ and its substituted version, string sums, slice terms and families, and finally the quadruple-sum series ChanQuadSum and the left side ChanQuadLHS for Chan's Eq. (10.15). Many auxiliary reindexing equivalences and summable-family structures are included.
--
